# Logical Model — Gold Layer
## Company Risk Intelligence Platform

> **Schema type:** Star (4 dimensions + 1 fact) · **Fact grain:** one row per company
> Every column below is mapped to its exact Silver source for lineage/documentation.

---

## Overview

The Gold layer collapses eight Silver tables (at mixed grains) into a single star at
**company grain**. Each Silver detail table is aggregated to one value per company, then
assembled into `fact_company_risk`, surrounded by four descriptive dimensions.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    DIM_COMPANY  ||--|| FACT_COMPANY_RISK : "company_id"
    DIM_DATE     ||--o{ FACT_COMPANY_RISK : "score_date_key"
    DIM_INDUSTRY ||--o{ FACT_COMPANY_RISK : "industry_id"
    DIM_OFFICER  ||--|| FACT_COMPANY_RISK : "officer_summary_id"
```

**Source summary**

| Gold table | Built from |
| --- | --- |
| `dim_company` | `silver.dim_company` + `silver.ch_overview` |
| `dim_date` | generated from `silver.yf_stock` date range |
| `dim_industry` | `silver.yf_info` (sector / industry) |
| `dim_officer` | `silver.ch_people` (+ `silver.dim_company`) |
| `fact_company_risk` | `silver.yf_info` (financial + market) · `silver.yf_stock` (market) · `silver.ch_overview` + `silver.ch_people` (governance) · `silver.yf_news` (news) |

---

## DIM 1 — `dim_company`

The central entity. One row per company. Carries all resolved identifiers + descriptive attributes.

| Column | Type | Key | Source (table.column) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `company_id` | STRING | **PK** | `dim_company.company_id` (= company_number) |
| `company_name` | STRING | | `dim_company.company_name` |
| `company_number` | STRING | | `dim_company.company_number` |
| `ticker` | STRING | | `dim_company.ticker` (real, e.g. AML.L) |
| `ticker_safe` | STRING | | `dim_company.ticker_safe` (e.g. AML_L) |
| `company_status` | STRING | | `ch_overview.company_status` |
| `company_type` | STRING | | `ch_overview.company_type` |
| `date_of_creation` | DATE | | `ch_overview.date_of_creation` |

**Build logic:** join `silver.dim_company` to `silver.ch_overview` on `company_number`.

---

## DIM 2 — `dim_date`

Calendar dimension. One row per day across the stock-history window.

| Column | Type | Key | Source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `date_key` | INT | **PK** | derived: `date_format(full_date,'yyyyMMdd')` |
| `full_date` | DATE | | generated from `yf_stock.trading_date` (min → max) |
| `day` | INT | | derived: `dayofmonth(full_date)` |
| `month` | INT | | derived: `month(full_date)` |
| `quarter` | INT | | derived: `quarter(full_date)` |
| `year` | INT | | derived: `year(full_date)` |
| `day_of_week` | STRING | | derived: `date_format(full_date,'EEEE')` |

**Build logic:** `sequence(min(trading_date), max(trading_date), interval 1 day)` then explode.

---

## DIM 3 — `dim_industry`

Classification axis for sector/industry comparison.

| Column | Type | Key | Source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `industry_id` | INT | **PK** | derived: surrogate (`row_number`) |
| `sector_name` | STRING | | `yf_info.sector` |
| `industry_name` | STRING | | `yf_info.industry` |

**Build logic:** distinct (`sector`, `industry`) pairs from `silver.yf_info`, numbered.

---

## DIM 4 — `dim_officer`

Company-level governance summary derived from officer records.

| Column | Type | Key | Source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `officer_summary_id` | STRING | **PK** | = `company_id` |
| `company_id` | STRING | FK → dim_company | via `silver.dim_company` |
| `board_size` | INT | | derived: `count(*)` of `ch_people` per company |
| `active_officers` | INT | | derived: count where `ch_people.is_active = true` |
| `resigned_officers` | INT | | derived: count where `ch_people.is_active = false` |
| `director_churn` | DOUBLE | | derived: `resigned_officers / board_size` |

**Build logic:** aggregate `silver.ch_people` grouped by `company_number`, join to `dim_company`.

> Note: `ch_people.is_active` is already derived in Silver (active officers carry `resigned_on = '-'`).

