## FACT — `fact_company_risk`

One row per company. Foreign keys to all four dimensions; measures grouped by risk pillar.

### Keys

| Column | Type | Key | Source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `company_id` | STRING | **PK, FK → dim_company** | `dim_company.company_id` |
| `score_date_key` | INT | FK → dim_date | derived: today as `yyyyMMdd` |
| `industry_id` | INT | FK → dim_industry | lookup via `yf_info.sector/industry` → `dim_industry` |
| `officer_summary_id` | STRING | FK → dim_officer | = `company_id` |

### Financial pillar — source: `silver.yf_info` (pre-computed ratios)

| Column | Type | Source / formula |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `debt_to_equity` | DOUBLE | `yf_info.debttoequity` |
| `current_ratio` | DOUBLE | `yf_info.currentratio` |
| `net_margin` | DOUBLE | `yf_info.profitmargins` |
| `revenue_growth` | DOUBLE | `yf_info.revenuegrowth` |
| `financial_score` | DOUBLE | derived: normalized 0–100 blend of the four above |

### Market pillar — source: `silver.yf_stock` + `silver.yf_info`

| Column | Type | Source / formula |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `annual_volatility` | DOUBLE | `yf_stock.close`: stddev(daily returns) × √252 |
| `max_drawdown` | DOUBLE | `yf_stock.close`: min(close / running-peak − 1) |
| `beta` | DOUBLE | `yf_info.beta` |
| `market_score` | DOUBLE | derived: normalized 0–100 blend |

### Governance pillar — source: `silver.ch_overview` + `dim_officer` (+ optional `yf_info` risk scores)

| Column | Type | Source / formula |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `company_age_years` | DOUBLE | from `ch_overview.date_of_creation` to today |
| `accounts_overdue` | INT | `ch_overview.accounts_overdue` (boolean → 0/1) |
| `director_churn` | DOUBLE | `dim_officer.director_churn` |
| `governance_score` | DOUBLE | derived: normalized 0–100 blend |

> Optional enrichment: `yf_info.overallrisk` / `yf_info.boardrisk` (Yahoo's 1–10 governance
> indicators) can be folded into `governance_score` as additional signals.

### News pillar — source: `silver.yf_news`

| Column | Type | Source / formula |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `news_volume` | INT | `count(*)` of articles per company |
| `news_sentiment` | DOUBLE | net positive/negative keyword score from `yf_news.title` |
| `news_score` | DOUBLE | derived: normalized 0–100 blend |

### Composite

| Column | Type | Source / formula |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `risk_score` | DOUBLE | `0.35·financial + 0.30·market + 0.25·governance + 0.10·news` |
| `risk_band` | STRING | High (≥66) / Medium (≥33) / Low (<33) |
| `score_date` | DATE | `current_date()` |

---

## Normalization & Scoring Notes

Each raw metric is min-max scaled to 0–100 **across the company universe** so pillars are
comparable. Orientation is set per metric so that **higher score = higher risk**:

| Metric | Direction | Treatment |
| --- | --- | --- |
| debt_to_equity, annual_volatility, beta, director_churn, accounts_overdue, news_volume | high = risky | mapped straight |
| current_ratio, net_margin, revenue_growth, company_age_years, news_sentiment, max_drawdown | high = safer | **inverted** |

`max_drawdown` is inverted because it is negative — a deeper (more negative) drawdown is riskier.

